      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T22:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The flag shouldn\u0027t really be called \"VCONN delay.\" The delay is an implementation detail of the PS8xxx driver. All that `tcpm_set_vconn` knows is that it should call `set_vconn` here despite the fact that `TCPC_FLAGS_CONTROL_VCONN` is not set.\n\nI\u0027d call this something like `TCPC_FLAGS_SET_VCONN_IN_SYNC` or `TCPC_FLAGS_FOLLOW_VCONN`. You can put a comment like, \"Call the driver\u0027s `set_vconn` function even when the TCPC does not control VCONN.\"",
      "revId": "c1d62563997ed6b490791e38a7cecd4890aba53e",
